.\" audiobook_qc.1 — manual page for the audiobook_qc scanner
.\" Generated for audiobook_qc v1.0
.\"
.TH AUDIOBOOK_QC 1 "2025" "audiobook_qc" "Audiobook Quality Control"
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH NAME
.\"
audiobook_qc \- detect and rank audio quality issues in a folder of WAV files
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\"
.B python\ main.py
.I FOLDER
.RB [ \-\-skip
.IR DETECTOR \&...]
.RB [ \-\-max\-primary
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-secondary
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-clipping\-threshold
.IR F ]
.RB [ \-\-click\-band\-low
.IR HZ ]
.RB [ \-\-click\-band\-high
.IR HZ ]
.RB [ \-\-click\-threshold
.IR F ]
.RB [ \-\-click\-max\-duration\-ms
.IR MS ]
.RB [ \-\-click\-merge\-ms
.IR MS ]
.RB [ \-\-plosive\-band\-low
.IR HZ ]
.RB [ \-\-plosive\-band\-high
.IR HZ ]
.RB [ \-\-plosive\-threshold
.IR F ]
.RB [ \-\-plosive\-max\-duration\-ms
.IR MS ]
.RB [ \-\-plosive\-merge\-ms
.IR MS ]
.RB [ \-\-noise\-window\-seconds
.IR S ]
.RB [ \-\-noise\-db\-threshold
.IR DB ]
.RB [ \-\-noise\-min\-separation
.IR S ]
.RB [ \-\-frame\-size
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-hop\-length
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-rolling\-median\-seconds
.IR S ]
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\"
.B audiobook_qc
walks a directory of
.B .wav
files, runs four broadband signal-processing detectors against each file,
globally ranks every detected event by severity, then writes two output
artefacts into the scanned folder:
.TP
.B qc_report.csv
Machine-readable CSV with all ranked events: global rank, severity tier,
filename, timestamp in seconds, timestamp in MM:SS format, issue type, and
severity score.
.TP
.B review.html
Browser-based interactive review interface.  Each event has an inline audio
player, playback controls, per-event notes field, checkbox selection, and an
"Export Selected" button that downloads a filtered CSV.
.PP
The four detectors are:
.TP
.B clipping
Finds runs of consecutive samples at or above the hard-clip ceiling
(default 0.998).  Very short runs (< 3 samples) are ignored.  Severity is
proportional to run length.
.TP
.B click
Bandpass-filters to the 2 500 – 10 000 Hz range, computes short-time RMS
with a rolling-median baseline, and flags frames where the RMS exceeds
5 × the local median.  Events shorter than 15 ms are retained; longer bursts
are discarded as non-click transients.  Nearby events within 150 ms are merged.
.TP
.B plosive
Same pipeline as the click detector, operating in the 20 – 180 Hz band with a
4× threshold and an 80 ms maximum duration.  Captures low-frequency mouth pops
and microphone thumps.
.TP
.B noise_floor_jump
Computes 1-second RMS windows across the file (in dB) and flags pairs of
adjacent windows that differ by more than 14 dB.  Enforces a minimum
10-second gap between reported events to avoid multiple flags for the same
environmental change.
.PP
After per-file detection the full event list is globally ranked by severity
score.  Events are split into a
.B primary
tier (highest severity, capped at 75 by default) and a
.B secondary
tier (next highest, capped at 200 by default).  Only ranked events appear in
the output files.
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH OPTIONS
.\"
.SS Positional
.TP
.I FOLDER
Path to the directory containing
.B .wav
files.  The directory is searched non-recursively.
.\"
.SS Detectors
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fIDETECTOR\fR [\fIDETECTOR\fR ...]
Disable one or more detectors.  Allowed values:
.BR clipping ,
.BR click ,
.BR plosive ,
.BR noise_floor_jump .
Repeat the flag or space-separate multiple names.
.\"
.SS Report caps
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-primary\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum number of primary-tier events written to the output files.
.RI "Default: " 75 .
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-secondary\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum number of secondary-tier events written to the output files.
.RI "Default: " 200 .
.\"
.SS Clipping detection
.TP
\fB\-\-clipping\-threshold\fR \fIF\fR
Absolute sample-value ceiling (0.0 – 1.0) above which a sample is
considered clipped.
.RI "Default: " 0.998 .
.\"
.SS Click detection
.TP
\fB\-\-click\-band\-low\fR \fIHZ\fR
Lower bound of the click bandpass filter in Hz.
.RI "Default: " 2500 .
.TP
\fB\-\-click\-band\-high\fR \fIHZ\fR
Upper bound of the click bandpass filter in Hz.
.RI "Default: " 10000 .
.TP
\fB\-\-click\-threshold\fR \fIF\fR
RMS-to-median-baseline ratio required to flag a frame as a click candidate.
Higher values mean fewer, more severe events are flagged.
.RI "Default: " 5.0 .
.TP
\fB\-\-click\-max\-duration\-ms\fR \fIMS\fR
Flagged runs longer than this duration (in milliseconds) are discarded because
they are too long to be clicks.
.RI "Default: " 15 .
.TP
\fB\-\-click\-merge\-ms\fR \fIMS\fR
Adjacent click events separated by less than this gap (in milliseconds) are
merged into a single event.
.RI "Default: " 150 .
.\"
.SS Plosive detection
.TP
\fB\-\-plosive\-band\-low\fR \fIHZ\fR
Lower bound of the plosive bandpass filter in Hz.
.RI "Default: " 20 .
.TP
\fB\-\-plosive\-band\-high\fR \fIHZ\fR
Upper bound of the plosive bandpass filter in Hz.
.RI "Default: " 180 .
.TP
\fB\-\-plosive\-threshold\fR \fIF\fR
RMS-to-median-baseline ratio required to flag a frame as a plosive candidate.
.RI "Default: " 4.0 .
.TP
\fB\-\-plosive\-max\-duration\-ms\fR \fIMS\fR
Flagged runs longer than this duration (in milliseconds) are discarded.
.RI "Default: " 80 .
.TP
\fB\-\-plosive\-merge\-ms\fR \fIMS\fR
Adjacent plosive events separated by less than this gap (in milliseconds) are
merged into a single event.
.RI "Default: " 200 .
.\"
.SS Noise-floor jump detection
.TP
\fB\-\-noise\-window\-seconds\fR \fIS\fR
Length of each RMS measurement window in seconds.
.RI "Default: " 1.0 .
.TP
\fB\-\-noise\-db\-threshold\fR \fIDB\fR
Minimum absolute dB difference between two adjacent windows that triggers a
noise-floor jump event.
.RI "Default: " 14.0 .
.TP
\fB\-\-noise\-min\-separation\fR \fIS\fR
Minimum time in seconds enforced between consecutive noise-floor jump events
in the same file.
.RI "Default: " 10.0 .
.\"
.SS DSP / framing
.TP
\fB\-\-frame\-size\fR \fIN\fR
FFT frame size in samples used by the click and plosive detectors.
Must be a power of two for best FFT performance.
.RI "Default: " 2048 .
.TP
\fB\-\-hop\-length\fR \fIN\fR
Hop (stride) between successive frames in samples.
Smaller values increase time resolution at the cost of speed.
.RI "Default: " 512 .
.TP
\fB\-\-rolling\-median\-seconds\fR \fIS\fR
Width of the rolling-median baseline estimator used by the click and plosive
detectors.  Wider values produce a smoother baseline; narrower values track
fast level changes more tightly.
.RI "Default: " 1.0 .
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH EXAMPLES
.\"
Scan a folder with default settings:
.PP
.RS 4
.B python main.py ./chapters
.RE
.PP
Skip noise-floor detection:
.PP
.RS 4
.B python main.py ./chapters --skip noise_floor_jump
.RE
.PP
Skip multiple detectors:
.PP
.RS 4
.B python main.py ./chapters --skip click plosive
.RE
.PP
Increase report limits and raise the click sensitivity:
.PP
.RS 4
.B python main.py ./chapters --max-primary 100 --max-secondary 300 --click-threshold 4.0
.RE
.PP
Tighter clipping threshold, louder noise-floor events only:
.PP
.RS 4
.B python main.py ./chapters --clipping-threshold 0.99 --noise-db-threshold 20.0
.RE
.PP
Adjust DSP to match a 44.1 kHz file with finer time resolution:
.PP
.RS 4
.B python main.py ./chapters --frame-size 1024 --hop-length 256
.RE
.PP
Focus only on clipping (skip everything else):
.PP
.RS 4
.B python main.py ./chapters --skip click plosive noise_floor_jump
.RE
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH OUTPUT FILES
.\"
Both output files are written into
.I FOLDER
and will overwrite any existing file with the same name.
.TP
.B qc_report.csv
Comma-separated values.  Columns:
.BR rank_global ", " tier ", " filename ", " timestamp_seconds ,
.BR timestamp_minsec ", " issue_type ", " severity_score .
.TP
.B review.html
Self-contained interactive HTML page.  No server required; open with any
modern browser.  Inline
.B <audio>
elements allow direct playback from the scanned folder.  Each row has
a free-text notes textarea and a checkbox.  The
.B Export Selected
button downloads a CSV of checked rows with notes appended.
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH ISSUE TYPES
.\"
.TP
.B clipping
Hard-clipped sample run.
.TP
.B click
Short high-frequency transient (electrical or mechanical interference).
.TP
.B plosive
Low-frequency mouth pop or microphone thump.
.TP
.B noise_floor_jump
Sudden environmental-noise-floor change between adjacent measurement windows.
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.\"
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Must include the repository root when invoking via
.BR "python main.py" ,
or install the package with
.BR "pip install -e ." .
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.\"
Python 3.11 or later.
.PP
Required packages: numpy, scipy, librosa, soundfile.
.PP
Install with:
.PP
.RS 4
.B pip install numpy scipy librosa soundfile
.RE
.\"
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH FILES
.\"
.TP
.B audiobook_qc/config.py
All compiled-in default constants.  Edit this file to permanently change
any default value.
.TP
.B audiobook_qc/detectors.py
Signal-processing algorithms for all four issue types.
.TP
.B audiobook_qc/scanner.py
Directory walker and per-file loader.
.TP
.B audiobook_qc/ranking.py
Global severity ranker and tier assignment.
.TP
.B audiobook_qc/report_csv.py
CSV report writer.
.TP
.B audiobook_qc/report_html.py
Interactive HTML report writer.
